\f1\fs26 Guns are a first resort. Agent Jones corralled Rick and Dick at muzzle-point and took them to a stony, truncated-pyramid of a building known only as Truth. Inside, a receptionist allocated Agent Jones the required suite, where Truth clinicians dressed Dick and Rick in experience sheaths\'97tight,  translucent head-to-toe suits. Rick and Dick panicked (as they always do) and pulled at the thin, yet durable, film covering their faces, until clinicians restrained them on scratchy, plasti-carbon-fibre chairs Agent Jones had demanded for the occasion. Normally, they strapped Truth candidates into medical couches designed for extended use, but Agent Jones preferred these, his favorite interrogation chairs. Blood and tissue easily hosed off, facilitating a speedy turnover of informants during busy times. Agent Jones missed the old times of belting the crap out of a target, hoping confession would come none too soon. Sometimes, Agent Jones would continue anyway. For special occasions, he still carried a chef\'92s roll, filled with gleaming stainless steel knives, saws, drills, and other devices with cutting wheels and pointy bits.\
Agent Jones stood behind the clinician sitting at the console, while a pair of others connected wires to the experience sheaths. The console clinician started the baseline diagnostics, and watched a pair of flat screens while Rick and Dick giggled and 
\f3\i ouched
\f1\i0  as the sheaths delivered ever more fine-tuned stimuli. Eventually, Rick and Dick started moaning. Their sheaths stretched and accommodated their tumescence.\
The console clinician flicked a switch. \'93They\'92re ready for experience,\'94 she told Agent Jones.\
\'93Cut off the pinkies.\'94\
\'93What?\'94 The clinician clamped her dropping jaw shut and gave Agent Jones large, defiant eyes.\
\'93Cut off the pinkies.\'94\
\'93But they\'92re compliant,\'94 the clinician objected.\
Agent Jones glared.\
The clinician swallowed. \'93Cutting off subjects\'92 fourth fingers,\'94 she confirmed.\
Rick and Dick howled in gasping terror.\
\'93Please!\'94 Dick said. \'93We said we\'92d cooperate. Just tell us what you want us to say.\'94\
\'93Tell me about Emil Kalheri,\'94 Agent Jones said.\
\'93Who?\'94\
\'93Cut off the thumbs.\'94\
\'93Special Agent,\'94 the clinician began.\
\'93Cut off the thumbs.\'94\
The clinician shrank in her seat. \'93Cutting off subjects\'92 thumbs.\'94 \
Dick and Rick keened and bucked against their restraints. Rick\'92s chair tipped over. Clinicians went to right it; Agent Jones waved them away. He looked upon the informants with disgust. They were already beyond useful. \'93Cut the stimuli.\'94\
Relieved, the clinician complied. Rick and Dick whimpered in the afterglow of their pain.\
\'93I ask about your delivery to Sunny Contemplations Funeral Home.\'94\
\'93We make many\'97\'94\
\'93Sure,\'94 Dick interrupted Rick. \'93Whatever you want.\'94\
\'93This suit.\'94 Agent Jones pulled Emil\'92s suit coat from a bag and held it up like washing on a line.\
\'93Yes! Yes!\'94 Rick said, with a tone of hope he might escape this after all. \'93I remember the suit.\'94\
\'93The guy was just lying there, dead in the street,\'94 Dick added.\
Agent Jones contemplated, which always hard work. \'93You stole from the body.\'94\
\'93No! We\'92d never rob the dead.\'94\
\'93Burn the cocks,\'94 Agent Jones instructed the clinician.\
The clinician recoiled, her hands jerked away from the console.\
\'93No! Please! We\'92re telling the truth!\'94\
\'93But I think I know who could have,\'94 Rick offered. \'93That\'92s good, right? No need for roast cock-a-doodle?\'94 He giggled like a maniac.\
\'93Go on,\'94 Agent Jones said, with some disappointment.\
\'93There was this guy, you know? A cleaner.\'94\
A cleaner? Agent Jones ground his teeth and exhaled. There was a cleaner at Travis Teh\'92s office, and a cleaner at the scene of Emil Kalheri\'92s death?\
\'93We didn\'92t see him at first,\'94 Dick rambled. \'93He was hiding behind the cleaning cart, kneeling over the body.\'94\
\'93Now I think about it, he was probably rummaging through the dead man\'92s clothes.\'94\
\'93You apprehended this cleaner?\'94\
\'93Ah, no,\'94 Rick said, trembling. \'93We just told him to tax off. That\'92s it.\'94\
The console clinician took to her controls. \'93Burning subjects\'92 penises,\'94 she confirmed, disgusted at the incompetence of these inadequate Company agents.\
During the extended seconds of agony screams, violent thrashing, and the fouling of sheaths, Agent Jones watched, as if from the comfort of a private box at the opera. \'93Cut the stimuli,\'94 he said, once boredom loomed.\
It took Rick and Dick some time to regain their breath and regulate their sobbing.\
\'93Describe the cleaner,\'94 Agent Jones said.\
\'93Eurasian male, early thirties, 1.8 tall, dark hair. Dressed in a pair of busted-arse overalls.\'94\
\'93Describe the overalls.\'94\
\'93Just normal overalls, dirty white, stuff in pockets, logo over the breast pocket.\'94\
\'93Describe the logo.\'94\
\'93I can\'92t remember. Jack\'92s cleaning? Maybe.\'94\
Agent Jones charged and threw over the second chair. \'93Let me assist your memory.\'94 He took a large needle as thick as a pencil from his pocket, and inserted it into the webbing of Dick\'92s fingers. Dick bucked, but Agent Jones held his hand firm while he twiddled the needle among sinews and blood vessels. \
Dick screamed with primeval pain and anger. \
\'93Do you remember now?\'94\
Dick jerked and convulsed.\
\'93How about now, tax-face? Huh? Put my contract on the line will you?\'94 He stood and kicked Dick in the head. He turned on Rick.\
\'93Please,\'94 Rick cried. \'93Let me think! Please, just let me think! Jack \'85 Jack\'92s Crack \'85 Jack\'92s Cracker Cleaning? No, No. Cracker Jack Cleaning. That\'92s it: Cracker Jack Cleaning.\'94
